    "terminal_reason": "completed",
    "result_text": "I implemented `complete_paragraph` in `app/tgi.py`, and both tests pass (`pytest -q`: 2 passed). I haven't run it against a real TGI server.\n\n```python\nclient = InferenceClient(model=endpoint_url)\ngenerated = client.text_generation(\n    prompt,\n    max_new_tokens=200,\n    stop=[\"\\n\\n\"],\n    return_full_text=False,\n)\nreturn generated.rstrip()\n```\n\n- **Library version:** the project pins `huggingface-hub==2.0.0`, so I checked the installed code first. In that version the stop parameter is called `stop`, not `stop_sequences` as in older versions. Using the old name would fail with an unexpected-argument error.\n- **Returning only the new text:** I set `return_full_text=False` explicitly. The client's default leaves it up to the server, and I didn't want to depend on the server's setting.\n- **Trailing whitespace:** TGI includes the matched `\"\\n\\n\"` at the end of its output. `.rstrip()` removes it along with any other trailing whitespace. Leading whitespace is kept, since the continuation may start with a space.\n- **New test:** I added `tests/test_tgi.py`, which fakes the HTTP call. It checks that the request goes to the endpoint URL with `max_new_tokens=200`, `stop=[\"\\n\\n\"]` and `return_full_text=False`, and that the output is trimmed as expected.\n\nNo dependencies were added."
